# ── Client-facing friendly paths (defensive) ──────────────────────────────
# The client portal is served at /portal.html. Clients (and stale emails,
# bookmarks, or typed URLs) land on /portal, /login, /signup, /account,
# /billing, /usage, /dashboard, /onboard, /app — none of which existed as
# files, producing Netlify default 404s. Redirect them all to the portal.
# Pretty-URL handling: /portal itself resolves via implicit pretty-URL
# rewrite, but is included explicitly for clarity and case variants.
/portal                      /portal.html          301
/portal/*                    /portal.html          301
/login                       /portal.html          301
/signup                      /portal.html          301
/account                     /portal.html          301
/billing                     /portal.html          301
/usage                       /portal.html          301
/dashboard                   /portal.html          301
